  "slug": "expanding-glycomics-0644",
  "summary": "Recent releases extend proteomics beyond peptide identification into proteoforms, phosphosite localization, and glycoproteomics data sharing.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread across these items is moving proteomics beyond routine peptide identification toward proteoform resolution, modification site assignment, and standardized glycan data. mE-DIA is a library-free multi-enzyme DIA-MS workflow with proteoform inference and a peptide mapper, reported to boost protein identifications by 30%. onsite provides open-source Python phosphosite localization with alanine-decoy FLR estimation across AScore, PhosphoRS and pyLucXor. SeekNSee offers rule-based, enzyme-aware proteotypic peptide prioritization with traceable scoring, while CasanovoGUI provides a desktop interface to Casanovo de novo sequencing. On the glycan side, GlycoPOST extends glycomics data sharing to glycoproteomics under updated MIRAGE guidelines, and GlyTouCan v4 revises the structure repository interface and REST API. The shared emphasis is usability and standardized infrastructure rather than any single new algorithm.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-11"
}
